    /**Release resource

Gives one resource back, whatever it is. What that means is the resource's own business: an SMS number goes back to the provider and is retired, a dedicated iMessage line goes back to the shared pool and stays in existence for someone else to claim. Either way the provider is contacted first where there is one, then a single transaction disables every ability, ends the project's hold and closes the charge period — so a provider that refuses leaves the resource exactly as it was, still owned and still billed. Usually finishes inside this request and answers 200; if the provider is slow it answers 202 and the Location points at the operation to poll. The decrement runs behind the answer either way, so the resource is gone when you are told it is. Takes no Idempotency-Key — releasing the same resource twice is the same request. Releasing one that is already gone answers 404. Requires the platforms:write permission bound to the project resource in the path.

Tags: Resources.

Response `200`: The release finished inside this request. The resource is gone.

Response `202`: The release is still running at the provider. GET the Location after the Retry-After interval; a terminal answer may arrive on any read.

Response `401`: NOT_AUTHENTICATED: Not Authenticated

Response `403`: FORBIDDEN: Forbidden; RESOURCE_MISMATCH: Resource Mismatch

FORBIDDEN: Forbidden; INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE: Insufficient Scope; ORGANIZATION_SSO_REQUIRED: Organization SSO Required

Response `404`: RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND: Resource Not Found

Response `409`: WHATSAPP_SENDER_CONNECTED: WhatsApp Sender Connected; WHATSAPP_SENDER_PROVISIONING: WhatsApp Sender Provisioning

Response `422`: VALIDATION_FAILED: Request Validation Failed

Response `429`: RATE_LIMITED: Too Many Requests

Response `500`: INVALID_AUTH_CONTEXT: Invalid Authentication Context

INTERNAL_ERROR: Internal Server Error

Response `502`: UPSTREAM_FAILURE: Upstream Service Failure

Response `503`: UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE: Upstream Service Unavailable

Response `504`: REQUEST_TIMEOUT: Request Timeout; UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT: Upstream Service Timeout*/
